  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3HARRIS Technologies recorded $312M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS Technologies won 188 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.7M and year-over-year change up 11.7%. L3HARRIS Technologies obligations this fiscal year follow a recent pattern of fluctuation: FY21 obligations were $436M, FY22 were $480M, FY23 were $543M, FY24 were $492M, and FY25 were $279M. L3HARRIS Technologies revenue is concentrated in a handful of markets. L3HARRIS Technologies generated $106M from Engineering Services, $66.3M from Custom Computer Programming Services, and $62.1M from Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS Technologies has two lead federal buyers so far: the Department of Transportation obligated $130M and the Department of Defense obligated $125M. L3HARRIS Technologies also received $54.9M from the Department of Commerce and smaller amounts from other agencies. This snapshot covers fiscal-year-to-date obligations and the current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of L3HARRIS Technologies?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $130M to L3HARRIS Technologies in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $125M. The Department of Commerce obligated $54.9M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.1M, and the Department of the Interior shows $0 in obligations this period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which product and service markets drive L3HARRIS Technologies federal obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market for L3HARRIS Technologies at $106M in FY2026 to date. Custom Computer Programming Services accounted for $66.3M, and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $62.1M. Other notable markets include Satellite Telecommunications at $23.4M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $16.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does L3HARRIS Technologies make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "L3HARRIS Technologies has $312M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS Technologies won 188 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $1.7M and year-over-year change up 11.7%. Historical annual obligations show FY21 at $436M, FY22 at $480M, FY23 at $543M, FY24 at $492M, and FY25 at $279M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from L3HARRIS Technologies?",
